    "b-ks2-src-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A knowledge source stores raw material cited by the knowledge graph. Every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row and every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that resolves to one record in one source. Sources hold records, and the graph holds claims. Citations use locators rather than foreign keys to source rows, with one pointer mechanism across five heterogeneous sources. Reverse lookup finds claims supported by a record through an indexed query on "
        },
        {
          "insert": "(kind, locator)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Display resolves a locator into its source at read time; no content snapshot is stored on the citing row."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-classes-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-classes-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Two Classes"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-classes-table": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-classes-table",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Class",
          "Sources",
          "Contract"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Archival",
            "Discord, pull requests, wiki",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Raw inputs, frozen once ingested. A new Discord export or PR import appends rows on the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "kg2-ingest",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " sync lane and gets them indexed; the wiki mirror is imported only on an explicit "
              },
              {
                "insert": "--lane wiki",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " request. It is never imported implicitly, including through "
              },
              {
                "insert": "--lane all",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ". Existing rows never change, so a locator into an archival source cannot drift and carries no digest."
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "Operational",
            "Attempts, code",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Attempts provide evidence from the target ledger. Runs, submissions, and transcripts grow with every run and are immutable once written. Code is the active checkout and the only drifting source. Its citations are the only ones that carry a required "
              },
              {
                "insert": "digest",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": "."
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-standards-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-standards-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Standards Sit Outside"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-standards-body": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-standards-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Standards are QA-owned rules with lints, injected at worker boot and enforced at the ship gate. They belong to the knowledge system but sit outside the knowledge graph. See "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Standards",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/30-knowledge/70-standards",
              "label": "Standards"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". They are not a knowledge source, not walkable, and never citable as evidence. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " enum has no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "standards",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " entry, and the omission is deliberate."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-grammar-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-grammar-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Locator Grammar"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-grammar-body": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-grammar-body",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The grammar is closed. The resolver rejects any locator that does not match its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "'s grammar or whose kind and scheme differ. A "
        },
        {
          "insert": "discord",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row with a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locator never resolves. Each form's payload is the store row's primary key. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the one kind with no store row. The checkout at "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<revision>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the store, and only there does a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of the span text pin what was read."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-grammar-table": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-grammar-table",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Kind",
